## AC-4 — engine support surface · PASS

**4a `--families`:**
```
cwd: /home/kupipi/Documents/git/strata
$ ./build-hip/strata --families
./build-hip/strata: error while loading shared libraries: libhipblas.so.3: cannot open
  shared object file: No such file or directory                              exit=127

$ LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/opt/rocm/core-10.1/lib ./build-hip/strata --families     exit=0
qwen4exp qwen35moe
```
**4b `--geometry`:**
```
cwd: /home/kupipi/Documents/git/strata
$ LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/opt/rocm/core-10.1/lib ./build-hip/strata --geometry     exit=0
flash_next
```
The exit-127 line is a **runtime loader path** issue (`ldd` shows `libhipblas.so.3`,
`librocblas.so.5`, `libhipblaslt.so.1`, `libamdhip64.so.7` as `not found` until the ROCm lib
dir is on `LD_LIBRARY_PATH`). It is NOT a link failure in the build: AC-3 exited 0 and the
binary is complete. `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` is an environment variable, not an install.

**Family list, transcribed:** `qwen4exp`, `qwen35moe`. These are the **GGUF architectures** this
build runs, not marketing names: `qwen4exp` **is** Qwen3.8-Flash-Next and `qwen35moe` **is**
Qwen3.6-35B-A3B (`serve/server.py:9695`, `strata_control/drafting.py:476`,
`strata_control/feed.py:153-155`; compiled in at `src/program/generate.cpp:3566-3574`, with
`qwen35moe` present because `cmake/strata_gpu_engine.cmake:545` sets `STRATA_HAVE_QWEN35=1`).
**The family the gfx1150 bench note (`bench/results/2026-10-07-community-gfx1150`) measured —
Qwen3.8-Flash-Next — is supported by this build, as `qwen4exp`.** The families **not**
implemented at `baf16363` are **Mixtral 8x7B**, **Qwen3-30B-A3B** and **DeepSeek**; the mapping
greps and their exit codes are in the RW-1 section of `artifacts/families.txt`. (`qwen35moe` is
Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, which is **not** Qwen3-30B-A3B.)
*Corrected by `RW-HO-STRATA-001-1` F1: an earlier version of this paragraph wrongly stated that
Qwen3.8-Flash-Next was not in this build's list. The transcribed output above is unchanged.*

Raw: `artifacts/families.txt`, `artifacts/geometry.txt`. Also `artifacts/help.txt` (`--help`,
